{"content_hash": "7020e46c2fb32874", "version_id": 834, "article_id": 84, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "The Weeknd samples Faye Wong, reviving a 1993 Cantonese song", "title_zh": "The Weeknd采样王菲，33年前粤语老歌翻红", "has_translation": true, "topic": "business", "source": "tmtpost", "source_url": "https://www.tmtpost.com/8188417.html", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1596633313465-1256feb1c6d9?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Nnx8d2Vla25kfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTM0OTIzMjJ8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Samuel Regan-Asante on Unsplash", "author": "Samuel Regan-Asante", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@reganography?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/black-wooden-shelf-with-books-5j7nQv-jaVM?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(73, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(111, 46%, 48%)", "label": "BUSINESS", "seed": "5d19934133bc"}}, "published_date": "2026-11-01", "word_count": 262, "reading_minutes": 1.3, "lead": "At his Hong Kong concert, The Weeknd surprised fans by sampling Faye Wong's 1993 song 'Seasonal Wind'. The moment has renewed interest in how far Wong's music has travelled beyond Asia.", "lead_zh": "在香港演唱会上，The Weeknd出人意料地采样了王菲1993年的《季候风》。这一刻让外界重新关注王菲的音乐究竟走得多远。", "preview": "On 24 October, The Weeknd opened his Hong Kong tour dates by releasing a city-exclusive track called 'Hong Kong'. Between psychedelic synths", "preview_zh": "10月24日，The Weeknd在香港巡演首场推出一首城市限定曲《Hong Kong》。在迷幻合成器和暗色R&B节奏之间，王菲空灵的粤语嗓音悄然浮现，两种跨时代的风格意外契合。此前他也为东京做过类似限定曲，采样了高桥洋子的作品。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 817, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/84/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 105.6, "size_bytes": 634608, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 317, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/84/en_b2_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 108.3, "size_bytes": 650736, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 317, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/84/en_b2_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/84/en_b2_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 115.025, "size_bytes": 691056, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 317, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/84/en_b2_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/84/en_b2_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 98.825, "size_bytes": 593856, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 317, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/84/en_b2_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/84/en_b2_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 105.8, "size_bytes": 635760, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 317, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/84/en_b2_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@1941809/content/data/versions/834.json", "paragraphs": ["On 24 October, The Weeknd opened his Hong Kong tour dates by releasing a city-exclusive track called 'Hong Kong'. Between psychedelic synths and dark R&B beats, Faye Wong's airy Cantonese voice appears quietly, and the two styles from different eras fit together surprisingly well. The Weeknd has made similar city songs before, including one for Tokyo that sampled Yoko Takahashi.", "Why Wong, and why this relatively lesser-known song? The Weeknd has shared Wong's 1996 album 'Fuzao' online and used 'Dream Lover' as background music in a recent post. The 'Hong Kong' video, directed with a strong 1980s Hong Kong film style, borrows heavily from Wong Kar-wai's 'Chungking Express'. The Weeknd is reportedly a huge fan of late-80s and early-90s Hong Kong cinema.", "Wong's overseas reach is often misunderstood. She never worked the Western market like some C-pop artists, yet she still draws about 1.42 million monthly listeners on Spotify. Her real commercial success came in Japan: in 1999 she became the first Chinese-language singer to hold a solo concert at Tokyo's Budokan, and her 'Final Fantasy VIII' theme 'Eyes on Me' reached No. 9 on the Oricon chart and sold over 500,000 copies there.", "In Europe and the US, Wong entered through film and alternative music rather than charts. 'Chungking Express' brought her global attention, and her 1994 covers of Cocteau Twins songs led to a rare collaboration with the band. Pitchfork has called 'Fuzao' a peak of experimental Chinese pop, and her albums remain staples on dream-pop listening lists.", "The Weeknd's sample does not prove Wong is a mainstream Western star."], "paragraphs_zh": ["10月24日，The Weeknd在香港巡演首场推出一首城市限定曲《Hong Kong》。在迷幻合成器和暗色R&B节奏之间，王菲空灵的粤语嗓音悄然浮现，两种跨时代的风格意外契合。此前他也为东京做过类似限定曲，采样了高桥洋子的作品。", "为什么选王菲，又为什么是这首相对冷门的歌？The Weeknd曾在网上分享王菲1996年的专辑《浮躁》，近日还以《梦中人》作配乐。走老港片风格的《Hong Kong》MV大量致敬王家卫的《重庆森林》。据报道，他是80年代末90年代初香港电影的超级影迷。", "王菲的海外影响力常被误解。她不像一些C-pop艺人那样经营欧美市场，但在Spotify仍有约142万月听众。真正的商业成绩在日本：1999年她成为首位在武道馆开个唱的华语歌手，《最终幻想VIII》主题曲《Eyes on Me》登上公信榜第9位，在日销量超过50万张。", "在欧美，王菲是靠电影和另类音乐而非榜单进入视野的。《重庆森林》让她获得国际关注，1994年翻唱Cocteau Twins的作品更促成双方罕见合作。Pitchfork称《浮躁》是华语实验流行的巅峰，她的专辑至今仍常出现在梦幻流行歌单上。", "The Weeknd的采样并不能证明王菲已是欧美主流明星。但它确实说明，当其他文化的创作者几十年后仍不断回望这些作品时，影响力可以持续更久。"], "body": "On 24 October, The Weeknd opened his Hong Kong tour dates by releasing a city-exclusive track called 'Hong Kong'. Between psychedelic synths and dark R&B beats, Faye Wong's airy Cantonese voice appears quietly, and the two styles from different eras fit together surprisingly well. The Weeknd has made similar city songs before, including one for Tokyo that sampled Yoko Takahashi.\n\nWhy Wong, and why this relatively lesser-known song? The Weeknd has shared Wong's 1996 album 'Fuzao' online and used 'Dream Lover' as background music in a recent post. The 'Hong Kong' video, directed with a strong 1980s Hong Kong film style, borrows heavily from Wong Kar-wai's 'Chungking Express'. The Weeknd is reportedly a huge fan of late-80s and early-90s Hong Kong cinema.\n\nWong's overseas reach is often misunderstood. She never worked the Western market like some C-pop artists, yet she still draws about 1.42 million monthly listeners on Spotify. Her real commercial success came in Japan: in 1999 she became the first Chinese-language singer to hold a solo concert at Tokyo's Budokan, and her 'Final Fantasy VIII' theme 'Eyes on Me' reached No. 9 on the Oricon chart and sold over 500,000 copies there.\n\nIn Europe and the US, Wong entered through film and alternative music rather than charts. 'Chungking Express' brought her global attention, and her 1994 covers of Cocteau Twins songs led to a rare collaboration with the band. Pitchfork has called 'Fuzao' a peak of experimental Chinese pop, and her albums remain staples on dream-pop listening lists.\n\nThe Weeknd's sample does not prove Wong is a mainstream Western star.", "body_zh": "10月24日，The Weeknd在香港巡演首场推出一首城市限定曲《Hong Kong》。在迷幻合成器和暗色R&B节奏之间，王菲空灵的粤语嗓音悄然浮现，两种跨时代的风格意外契合。此前他也为东京做过类似限定曲，采样了高桥洋子的作品。\n\n为什么选王菲，又为什么是这首相对冷门的歌？The Weeknd曾在网上分享王菲1996年的专辑《浮躁》，近日还以《梦中人》作配乐。走老港片风格的《Hong Kong》MV大量致敬王家卫的《重庆森林》。据报道，他是80年代末90年代初香港电影的超级影迷。\n\n王菲的海外影响力常被误解。她不像一些C-pop艺人那样经营欧美市场，但在Spotify仍有约142万月听众。真正的商业成绩在日本：1999年她成为首位在武道馆开个唱的华语歌手，《最终幻想VIII》主题曲《Eyes on Me》登上公信榜第9位，在日销量超过50万张。\n\n在欧美，王菲是靠电影和另类音乐而非榜单进入视野的。《重庆森林》让她获得国际关注，1994年翻唱Cocteau Twins的作品更促成双方罕见合作。Pitchfork称《浮躁》是华语实验流行的巅峰，她的专辑至今仍常出现在梦幻流行歌单上。\n\nThe Weeknd的采样并不能证明王菲已是欧美主流明星。但它确实说明，当其他文化的创作者几十年后仍不断回望这些作品时，影响力可以持续更久。", "text": "On 24 October, The Weeknd opened his Hong Kong tour dates by releasing a city-exclusive track called 'Hong Kong'. Between psychedelic synths and dark R&B beats, Faye Wong's airy Cantonese voice appears quietly, and the two styles from different eras fit together surprisingly well. The Weeknd has made similar city songs before, including one for Tokyo that sampled Yoko Takahashi. Why Wong, and why this relatively lesser-known song? The Weeknd has shared Wong's 1996 album 'Fuzao' online and used 'Dream Lover' as background music in a recent post. The 'Hong Kong' video, directed with a strong 1980s Hong Kong film style, borrows heavily from Wong Kar-wai's 'Chungking Express'. The Weeknd is reportedly a huge fan of late-80s and early-90s Hong Kong cinema. Wong's overseas reach is often misunderstood. She never worked the Western market like some C-pop artists, yet she still draws about 1.42 million monthly listeners on Spotify. Her real commercial success came in Japan: in 1999 she became the first Chinese-language singer to hold a solo concert at Tokyo's Budokan, and her 'Final Fantasy VIII' theme 'Eyes on Me' reached No. 9 on the Oricon chart and sold over 500,000 copies there. In Europe and the US, Wong entered through film and alternative music rather than charts. 'Chungking Express' brought her global attention, and her 1994 covers of Cocteau Twins songs led to a rare collaboration with the band. Pitchfork has called 'Fuzao' a peak of experimental Chinese pop, and her albums remain staples on dream-pop listening lists. The Weeknd's sample does not prove Wong is a mainstream Western star.", "vocab": [{"word": "sample", "pos": "verb", "zh": "采样（音乐）", "note": "音乐制作中截取他人作品片段", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "exclusive", "pos": "adj", "zh": "专属的，限定的", "note": "city-exclusive 城市限定", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "psychedelic", "pos": "adj", "zh": "迷幻的", "note": "常形容音效或视觉风格", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "airy", "pos": "adj", "zh": "空灵的", "note": "形容嗓音轻盈通透", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "relatively", "pos": "adv", "zh": "相对地", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "reach", "pos": "noun", "zh": "影响力，覆盖面", "note": "overseas reach 海外影响力", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "misunderstand", "pos": "verb", "zh": "误解", "note": "被动式 is often misunderstood", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "commercial", "pos": "adj", "zh": "商业的", "note": "commercial success 商业成绩", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "alternative", "pos": "adj", "zh": "另类的", "note": "alternative music 另类音乐", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "collaboration", "pos": "noun", "zh": "合作", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "mainstream", "pos": "adj", "zh": "主流的", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "body of work", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "全部作品，作品体系", "note": "指某位创作者的整体作品", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "fetched_at": "2026-11-01T00:18:40.801393", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "On", "s": 0.25, "e": 0.375, "sm": 250, "em": 375, "cs": 0, "ce": 2, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "24", "s": 0.375, "e": 0.9, "sm": 375, "em": 900, "cs": 3, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "October", "s": 0.9, "e": 1.575, "sm": 900, "em": 1574, "cs": 6, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": ",", "s": 1.575, "e": 1.675, "sm": 1575, "em": 1675, "cs": 13, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "The", "s": 1.675, "e": 1.775, "sm": 1675, "em": 1774, "cs": 15, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "Weeknd", "s": 1.775, "e": 2.125, "sm": 1775, "em": 2125, "cs": 19, "ce": 25, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "opened", "s": 2.125, "e": 2.438, "sm": 2125, "em": 2437, "cs": 26, "ce": 32, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "his", "s": 2.438, "e": 2.6, "sm": 2437, "em": 2600, "cs": 33, "ce": 36, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "Hong", "s": 2.6, "e": 2.875, "sm": 2600, "em": 2874, "cs": 37, "ce": 41, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "Kong", "s": 2.875, "e": 3.15, "sm": 2875, "em": 3149, "cs": 42, "ce": 46, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "tour", "s": 3.15, "e": 3.375, "sm": 3150, "em": 3375, "cs": 47, "ce": 51, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "dates", "s": 3.375, "e": 3.938, "sm": 3375, "em": 3937, "cs": 52, "ce": 57, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "